  "disclaimer": "Demo profile, not a real fund. On-chain evidence is real Stellar testnet data from Invaria's own DEMOA issuance; order, bank and transfer-agent records are synthetic. Exact match, no fees, no rounding and the authorities are fixture decisions. Owner decision 2026-10-05: the on-chain source only requires provider_claimed coverage (Horizon and RPC are both operated by SDF, so no independent verification exists yet); institutional sources still require internally_checked. Rules of 1.3.0 (ADR-014, ADR-015), unchanged: the on-chain coverage declares its quarantine policy (a quarantined record never credits fulfilment and makes UNKNOWN only what resolving it could change; a certificate's quarantine stays active until one of the same chain scope explicitly supersedes it; a record's nature and ledger operation are relied on only when the snapshot supports them); a movement to a muxed (M) sub-account is attributed only by an IdentityLink naming that M address, and one no link attributes is never counted, though it is not thereby foreign; a transaction memo never links evidence to an operation. Version 1.4.0 (INV-013 closure, ADR-015 M2): the on-chain source admits explicitly, besides the Classic payment mapping 1.1.0 of its authoritative movements, every mapping with which the adapter writes the other records of the source (additional_mapping_refs); a new evaluation refuses evidence produced by a mapping the profile does not admit for its source, and nothing is relabelled.",
